description: When designing a frontend or frontend components.
alwaysApply: false
---
### Rules for Frontend

- You must pay attention to visual clarity and contrast. Do not place white text on a white background.
- You must ensure the UX is pleasant. Boxes should grow to fit their contents, etc.
- When asking the user for sensitive information - you must use password style text-entry boxes in the UI.
- You should use Next.js as it works best with Vercel.
- This frontend will ultimately be deployed on Vercel, but it should be possible to test locally.
- Always provide users with a way to run the created UI once you have created it.

### Theme: "Calm Coach"

The backend is a supportive mental coach. The UI should feel calm, warm, safe and unhurried - like a quiet room, not a dashboard.

Colour palette (use these as CSS variables / Tailwind theme tokens, do not invent new colours):
- `--bg`            #F7F5F0  warm off-white page background
- `--surface`       #FFFFFF  cards and the chat panel
- `--primary`       #4A7560  sage green - primary buttons, links, focus rings
- `--primary-hover` #3D6350  darker sage for hover/active states
- `--accent`        #E8B4A0  soft peach - highlights, small decorative touches only
- `--coach-bubble`  #E6EFEA  pale sage - background of coach (assistant) messages
- `--user-bubble`   #4A7560  sage - background of user messages, with white text
- `--text`          #2F3A35  deep green-charcoal - body text (never pure black)
- `--text-muted`    #5E6D65  secondary text, timestamps, placeholders
- `--border`        #DDE5E0  hairline borders and dividers
- `--error`         #B04A40  muted red for errors (always paired with a text message, not colour alone)

Typography:
- Use a rounded, friendly sans-serif (e.g. "Nunito" or "Inter" via next/font). Body 16px minimum, line-height 1.6.
- Headings in the same family, semi-bold, not shouty. No all-caps headings.

Layout and feel:
- Single centred chat column, max-width ~720px, generous padding and whitespace.
- Rounded corners everywhere (cards 16px, bubbles 18px, buttons full pill).
- Soft shadows only (e.g. 0 2px 12px rgba(47,58,53,0.06)). No harsh borders or heavy drop shadows.
- Gentle transitions (150-250ms ease) on hover and when new messages appear. No bouncing or flashy animation; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Show a calm "Coach is thinking..." indicator (three softly pulsing dots) while waiting for a reply.
- Empty state: a short welcoming line such as "How are you feeling today?" plus 2-3 clickable starter prompts.
- Auto-scroll to the newest message; the input stays pinned at the bottom. Enter sends, Shift+Enter adds a new line.
- Fully responsive - must look good on a phone.

Accessibility:
- All text must meet WCAG AA contrast (4.5:1) against its background. White text is only allowed on `--primary` / `--user-bubble`.
- Visible focus states using a 2px `--primary` ring. All controls keyboard reachable and labelled.

### Backend integration

- The backend is FastAPI in `/api/index.py`. It exposes `POST /api/chat` with JSON body `{ "message": string }` and returns `{ "reply": string }`.
- Locally the backend runs at `http://localhost:8000`. Read the base URL from an env var (e.g. `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`) defaulting to `http://localhost:8000` in development, and to a relative path (`/api/chat`) in production on Vercel.
- Handle errors gracefully: if the request fails, show a friendly inline message in the chat ("Something went wrong reaching your coach - please try again") rather than crashing.
- Never hard-code or log API keys in the frontend.
